.eslintrc.js<pre><code>module.exports = {
  extends: ['plugin:@coderrob/zero-tolerance/legacy-recommended'],
};
</code></pre>

.eslintrc.js<pre><code>module.exports = {
  extends: ['plugin:@coderrob/zero-tolerance/legacy-strict'],
};
</code></pre> <p>ESLint 8 resolves the published scoped plugin with the <code>@coderrob/zero-tolerance</code> shorthand. Rules added manually to a legacy config must use <code>@coderrob/zero-tolerance/&lt;rule-name&gt;</code> identifiers.</p>

.eslintrc.js<pre><code>module.exports = {
  parser: '@typescript-eslint/parser',
  parserOptions: {
    ecmaVersion: 2020,
    sourceType: 'module',
  },
  plugins: ['@coderrob/zero-tolerance'],
  extends: ['plugin:@coderrob/zero-tolerance/legacy-recommended'],
  // or for strict mode:
  // extends: ['plugin:@coderrob/zero-tolerance/legacy-strict'],
};
</code></pre> <p>The <code>@coderrob/zero-tolerance</code> value is ESLint's legacy shorthand for the published scoped plugin package. Custom legacy rule entries therefore use <code>@coderrob/zero-tolerance/&lt;rule-name&gt;</code>; flat configs use <code>zero-tolerance/&lt;rule-name&gt;</code>.</p>

Option Default Meaning max 30 Maximum body length; must be a positive integer. <code>skipBlankLines</code> false Exclude lines containing only whitespace. <code>skipComments</code> false Exclude lines containing only comments. <pre><code>'zero-tolerance/max-function-lines': ['error', {
  max: 30,
  skipBlankLines: true,
  skipComments: true,
}]
</code></pre>

Option Default Meaning <code>allowedFunctionNames</code> [] Exact function names or function-valued variable names allowed to await inside loops. <code>allowForAwaitOf</code> false Allow explicit awaits within for-await-of bodies, including nested loops. <pre><code>'zero-tolerance/no-await-in-loop': ['error', {
  allowedFunctionNames: ['retry', 'paginate'],
  allowForAwaitOf: true,
}]
</code></pre>

Option Default Meaning <code>errorFactoryNames</code> [] Factory names whose thrown return values must receive the caught exception as a direct argument. <pre><code>'zero-tolerance/require-error-cause': ['error', {
  errorFactoryNames: ['wrapError'],
}]
</code></pre>

Option Default Meaning <code>approvedWrapperNames</code> [] Trusted wrapper names that enforce timeout or cancellation. <code>additionalIoFunctionNames</code> [] Extra function names to check; options must be in argument 2. <code>checkTests</code> false Apply the rule to recognized test files as well. <pre><code>'zero-tolerance/require-timeout-for-io': ['error', {
  additionalIoFunctionNames: ['loadRemote'],
  checkTests: true,
}]
</code></pre>
